# The build context of demo/Dockerfile is the repository (compose.override.yaml, the CI lanes), read through this list
# alone (BuildKit takes <Dockerfile>.dockerignore over the context's .dockerignore). Nothing is sent but what is named
# here: the demo, the kit's recipes as the demo reads them (each recipe's manifest, README, templates, assets, PHP and
# config), the root files the gallery reads at run time, and tools/sync-demo, which the production build runs.
#
# Two rules of this format shape it. A pattern names a path, not a type, and loses a trailing slash: `!*/config/`
# would also take the file .git/config. And excluding a directory does not exclude the files inside it once an
# exception (`!…`) could match them. So a recipe's re-includes start with a letter or a digit (never a dot directory),
# and every exclusion names its directory and everything below it (`x` and `x/**`).
*

# the kit as the demo reads it (app.kit_dir: the demo's parent); a recipe's directories are those its copy-files names
!manifest.json
!kit.css
!INSTALL.md
!llms.txt
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!docs/GUIDE.md
![a-z0-9]*/manifest.json
![a-z0-9]*/README.md
![a-z0-9]*/templates
![a-z0-9]*/assets
![a-z0-9]*/src
![a-z0-9]*/config

# the demo app, without what is installed, built or local to a machine
!demo
demo/var
demo/var/**
demo/vendor
demo/vendor/**
demo/public/assets
demo/public/assets/**
demo/public/bundles
demo/public/bundles/**
demo/assets/vendor
demo/assets/vendor/**
demo/tests
demo/tests/**
demo/.env.local
demo/.env.test
demo/.editorconfig
demo/.gitignore
demo/.env.local.php
demo/.env.*.local
demo/compose*.yaml
demo/Dockerfile*
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store

# never, below any re-include above: dot directories (.git, .github…), tests, node packages, the Composer package
.*
.*/**
**/.git
**/.git/**
*/tests
*/tests/**
tests
tests/**
**/node_modules
**/node_modules/**
packages
packages/**

# copies the recipes into the demo at build time (removed from the production image after)
tools
tools/**
!tools/sync-demo
